                <pb facs="0950" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-25T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 25,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Your February 2, 11 a.m. and Department’s January 31, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department has requested Navy Department to issue orders for an officer and
                    Marines of the Legation Guard in Managua to proceed to territory from which
                    revolutionary activities are directed against Honduras. These Marines will be
                    instructed not to enter Honduran territory but to make a thorough investigation
                    of alleged activities by Honduran revolutionists. You will receive appropriate
                    instructions as soon as Navy Department informs this Department that orders to
                    the Marines have been issued.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
